we start with the end of a long campaign  tomorrow is  election day thousands of you will head  to the ballots tomorrow  but you can still drop off your mail-in  ballot today we have bianca holman live  with us  to share some of those last minute  reminders bianca  even though early in-person voting ended  on friday you can still put your ballot  in the mail  or drop it off in person at the clark  county elections office in north las  vegas  now because of the pandemic more than a  million people have voted by mail or  cast their ballots during the early  voting period  all active and registered voters were  sent their ballots in late september  or early october the elections office  still expects a big turnout on tuesday  monday we only have one facility  available it's only here at our office  965 trade drive  we'll be completely focused on making  sure that we're ready for election day  on election day the full vote center  allocation will be providing that and  yes we do expect  a number of voters to take advantage of  that a reminder to all voters  do not wait in line with those who are  wanting to vote in person  come to the front there'll be a staffer  there with a ballot box to make sure  it's sealed and that you've signed it  now once your ballot is in the mail or  dropped off you will not receive a  confirmation there are tools however for  you to check  the status of the ballot the secretary  of state offers a ballot tracker and the  elections department offers registered  voter  services on the website you can log in  and check the status  of the mail ballot or call 702 455  vote again if you'd like to drop off  your ballot in person today you can do  so  at the elections office in north las  vegas or of course you can wait till  tomorrow on tuesday to drop it off at  any polling location  and of course we will again be having  updates throughout the day reporting  bianca holman 8 news now
 

